/* Glyphs. Lucide's 24px set, rescaled to the handoff's 19px / 1.9 / no fill;
 * `splice` is drawn to match because no general set carries it.
 *
 * THE STROKE IS RE-CUT, NOT JUST RESCALED, AND THAT IS ARITHMETIC. The plan
 * said Lucide's 24/2.0 "rescales to the handoff's 19px / 1.9 without
 * redrawing". It does not: 19/24 x 2.0 = 1.58, which is 17% under spec.
 * Lucide's native stroke-to-size ratio is 0.0833 and the handoff's is 0.1, so
 * the rasteriser substitutes stroke-width 2.4 into the 24 viewBox and 19px
 * lands on 1.90 exactly. Checked by eye at both weights before choosing: at
 * 2.0 the marks read thin beside their bold 10px nav labels, and at 2.4
 * nothing muddies - the gem's facets and the stopwatch's dial, the two
 * densest here, keep their interior white at 19px. The SOURCES stay at
 * Lucide's 2.0 so all thirteen are one homogeneous set; the re-cut is a
 * rasteriser transform, applied uniformly, like the colour below.
 *
 * LICENCE IS ISC, NOT MIT - the plan said MIT and the file it tells you to
 * fetch says "ISC License" on line 1. Three of these thirteen (`check`,
 * `back`, `lock`) are Lucide's Feather-derived set and carry Feather's MIT
 * on top. Both texts are in LICENSE-lucide.txt beside the rasters.
 *
 * RASTER, NOT VECTOR. UI Toolkit reads SVG only through the Vector Graphics
 * package, and ad7ff3c removed two unused packages from the client build this
 * phase last. A dependency for glyphs that never exceed 24px is not a trade
 * worth making, so these are 3x PNGs: 57px authored, 19px drawn.
 *
 * AUTHORED WHITE, NOT BLACK, AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING.
 * -unity-background-image-tint-color MULTIPLIES the texture. Lucide's
 * `stroke="currentColor"` rasterises to black, black times any tint is
 * still black, and the two tab states at the bottom of this file would have
 * collapsed into one identical grey-on-nothing glyph with no error anywhere.
 * The rasteriser substitutes white for currentColor; the tint is what
 * colours a glyph, so every colour here still comes from the token layer.
 */
.icon {
    width: 19px;
    height: 19px;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: var(--mute-soft);
}
.icon--map     { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/map.png"); }
.icon--ark     { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/ark.png"); }
.icon--splice  { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/splice.png"); }
.icon--lab     { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/lab.png"); }
.icon--allies  { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/allies.png"); }
.icon--back    { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/back.png"); }
.icon--charge  { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/charge.png"); }
.icon--shard   { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/shard.png"); }
.icon--tier    { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/tier.png"); }
.icon--timer   { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/timer.png"); }
.icon--lock    { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/lock.png"); }
.icon--check   { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/check.png"); }
.icon--warning { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/warning.png"); }

/* Three more, and all three are BESPOKE rather than fetched - so all three
 * keep their .svg beside the raster, on the rule the thirteen established
 * (splice.svg was kept for exactly this reason; lucide.dev is a durable
 * source and a hand-drawn mark has none). Same pipeline, same re-cut:
 *
 *     sed 's/currentColor/#ffffff/g; s/stroke-width="2"/stroke-width="2.4"/g' n.svg \
 *       | rsvg-convert -w 57 -h 57 -o n.png
 *
 * `sparkle` IS THE HANDOFF'S OWN PATH, to the digit - the mutation banner in
 * `Splice Chamber.dc.html` draws
 * `M12 2 L14.5 9.5 L22 12 L14.5 14.5 L12 22 L9.5 14.5 L2 12 L9.5 9.5 Z`.
 * Lucide has a `sparkle`, and it is a different four-pointed star; the
 * handoff drew this one, so this is the one.
 *
 * THE TWO ARROWS ARE FILLED, WHICH BREAKS THIS SET'S `fill="none"` RULE ON
 * PURPOSE. The handoff's stat cells set them as literal text triangles - `▲`
 * at #6cba8b and `▼` at #e5867a, 10px beside a 15px value - and an outlined
 * chevron at that size reads as a chevron, which in this app means
 * navigation. A solid triangle at 11px reads as a direction. They keep the
 * set's rounded joins so they still belong to it. */
.icon--sparkle { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/sparkle.png"); }

/* THE TINT IS PART OF THE MARK HERE, AND NOT PART OF THE INFORMATION.
 * Direction is what says up or down - bible 10.4, colour never carries
 * information alone - and green/coral is the reinforcement the handoff
 * draws. Set on the modifier rather than left to each caller because a stat
 * cell that forgot it would get `.icon`'s --mute-soft and read as a
 * disabled arrow. --green (#7cc492) is the nearest token to the handoff's
 * #6cba8b and --coral (#e5867a) is its down arrow exactly.
 *
 * AFTER `.icon`, DELIBERATELY. These two ties with it on specificity (one
 * class each), and within a single stylesheet the later rule wins - which
 * is why they are here and not in a sheet whose load order against this one
 * nothing states. */
.icon--trend-up   { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/trend-up.png");
                    -unity-background-image-tint-color: var(--green); }
.icon--trend-down { background-image: url("project:///Assets/UI/Art/icons/trend-down.png");
                    -unity-background-image-tint-color: var(--coral); }

/* The tab bar's two states, per the handoff's nav model - plus the one rule
 * that keeps the glyph off the word.
 *
 * OUT OF FLOW, DELIBERATELY. A Button draws its `text` itself, centred in
 * its own content box, and an inserted child is not a flex sibling of that
 * text - in flow the two share the same space and the mark sits on the
 * label's first letters. Taking the glyph out of flow leaves the content box
 * holding nothing but the text, so the band Shell.uss reserves with
 * `padding-top: 31px` is the text's floor and this `top` is the glyph's
 * home inside it: 8px down, 19px tall, 4px of air, then the 10px label.
 *
 * `align-self` rather than left/right: the mark is a fixed 19px, so
 * stretching it is not available and `left: 0` would pin it to the padding
 * edge. Centre on the cross axis instead and it sits over the middle of the
 * word whatever the tab's width. */
.tab-bar__tab .icon {
    position: absolute;
    top: var(--space-2);
    align-self: center;
    -unity-background-image-tint-color: var(--mute-soft);
}
.tab-bar__tab--active .icon    { -unity-background-image-tint-color: var(--violet-text); }
